---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Enterprise Java Modernization | Shibu S"
  description="An architecture perspective on incremental modernization of enterprise Java applications."
>
  <article class="container section prose">
    <a class="text-link" href={`${base}#portfolio`}>
      ← Back to selected work
    </a>

    <p class="eyebrow">Architecture perspective</p>
    <h1>Modernizing enterprise Java applications</h1>

    <p class="notice">
      This article describes a general architecture approach,
      not a disclosed client implementation.
    </p>

    <h2>Start with the business problem</h2>
    <p>
      Establish the reasons for modernization: release delays,
      operational risk, scaling constraints, or high maintenance effort.
      Define measurable outcomes before selecting technologies.
    </p>

    <h2>Understand the existing system</h2>
    <p>
      Map business capabilities, integration dependencies, data ownership,
      and operational constraints. Identify where incremental change
      is feasible and where additional preparation is required.
    </p>

    <h2>Modernize incrementally</h2>
    <p>
      Prioritize a bounded capability, establish clear interfaces,
      and validate its behavior before expanding the migration.
      Retain a rollback strategy during transition.
    </p>

    <h2>Build operational foundations</h2>
    <p>
      Include automated testing, observability, security controls,
      deployment automation, and ownership responsibilities
      in the modernization plan.
    </p>

    <h2>Use AI with verification</h2>
    <p>
      Evaluate AI assistance for code explanation, test generation,
      and repetitive migration work. Keep engineers accountable
      for correctness, security, and business behavior.
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>